-- help-usage.txt --
Show what the status line last reported about each account's usage limits (5-hour and
7-day windows), when it last hit a limit, and the best account to continue with in this repository.

Usage is recorded by the status line, so it needs a one-time setup per settings file:
squadrn usage --setup wraps the status line command (your own one keeps running and showing).

Usage:
  squadrn usage [<account>] [flags]

Examples:
  squadrn usage                 all accounts
  squadrn usage work            details of claude/work
  squadrn usage --setup --all   record usage for every account
  squadrn usage --setup --undo  restore the previous status line

Flags:
      --all       with --setup: every account
  -h, --help      help for usage
      --json      print JSON
      --refresh   query login status, plan and organisation again
      --setup     record usage through the account's status line
      --undo      with --setup: restore the previous status line
      --watch     redraw every 5 seconds
  -y, --yes       do not ask for confirmation

Global Flags:
  -a, --account string   account to run as (provider/name or name)
  -C, --dir string       run as if started in this directory
      --no-color         disable colors (also: NO_COLOR=1)
